  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nRight now, in all browsers `<video autoplay muted>` will auto play even if the user has indicated they prefer reduced motion.\n\nThis is somewhat reasonable, as it isn't \"prefer no motion\", but in many cases the developer would wish to respect this preference.\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\n[You can use JavaScript](https://jsbin.com/futapiz/edit?html,output).\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nSomething like `<video autoplay=\"unless-prefers-reduced-motion\">`. Perhaps there's a shorter acceptable name.\n\nThis means the video will autoplay unless the user has indicted they prefer reduced motion, as `(prefers-reduced-motion)` in CSS.\n\n`HTMLMediaElement.autoplay` would return `false` if the attribute isn't present, `\"unless-prefers-reduced-motion\"` if the attribute is `\"unless-prefers-reduced-motion\"` and the element is a `video`, otherwise `true`.",
